# trufflehog path exclusions — declared fixtures, not blanket suppression.
#
# Read this before adding a line. The point of this file is that a REAL leak stands
# out against it. Every entry names why the path is a fixture, so a future reader can
# tell a deliberate test credential from a mistake. An undocumented entry defeats the
# file's whole purpose.
#
# Regex, one per line, matched against the file path.
#
# Scope note: run trufflehog over git-tracked files only. A full-tree scan returns
# ~994 findings against ~95 for tracked files, because it walks .afm-image/*.tar.gz
# container images, ci-reports-2*/ archives, __pycache__/*.pyc and AI session caches
# — none of which are tracked, and all of which are already gitignored.
#
# Detector note: the Lob detector must be excluded via --exclude-detectors, not here.
# It matches any `test_`-prefixed alphanumeric run, so it fires on every Python test
# function name in the repo (`test_cgroup_bridge_resolves_this_process` and 74 more).
# Excluding by path would also hide real findings in those same test files.

# ── Local development stack credentials ──────────────────────────────────────
# A self-consistent dev fixture set: components/backend/base/postgres.yaml SETS the
# password that the archivista client then connects with, so both halves are fixtures
# and neither is a credential for anything that exists. Confirmed as a test password.
# If a real deployment ever needs these, the repo already uses OpenBao via
# vault.hashicorp.com/agent-inject in 12 files — that is the target, not this file.
d2-osramp-apps/components/backend/.*/archivista-secret\.yaml$
d2-osramp-apps/components/backend/base/postgres\.yaml$
d2-osramp-apps/components/backend/.*/postgres-secret\.yaml$
d2-osramp-apps/components/frontend/base/archiver\.yaml$

# fe-signalloom local stack: signalloom/signalloom against an in-cluster service DNS
# name. Same reasoning — the manifest that sets it and the manifest that reads it are
# both in-repo fixtures.
d2-signalloom/apps/fe-signalloom/base/secrets\.yaml$

# ── Test fixtures that deliberately contain credential-shaped strings ────────
# These suites assert that the product REFUSES or REDACTS credentials, so they must
# contain realistic ones to be meaningful. Removing the strings would remove the test.
# See test_negative_security.py, whose guard fixture is literally
# `python3\0agent.py\0--token=SECRET_BEARER_TOKEN\0`.
d2-signalloom/apps/agentmaxxing-host-sensor/test_.*\.py$
d2-signalloom/apps/fe-signalloom/src/tests/.*\.py$
olly-replica/apps/sentinel/tests/.*\.py$
d2-signalloom/apps/signal-ingest/identity/.*_test\.go$
olly-replica/components/configs/base/seed/injection-corpus\.ndjson$

# ── Evidence documents ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Card proofs quote command output verbatim, including connection strings from the
# fixtures above. The quoting is the evidence; redacting it would break the audit
# trail these documents exist to provide.
docs/signalloom/.*-proof\.md$
docs/signalloom/.*-evidence\.md$
docs/signalloom/sfdp-p3-3-archivista-evidence\.md$

# ── NOT excluded, deliberately ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# .kind/ was removed from tracking and gitignored rather than excluded here. It is
# machine-local state regenerated by every `kind create`, pointing at an ephemeral
# localhost port, and carrying client key material. Because the gate scans
# `git archive HEAD`, untracked paths never reach it — so no exclusion is needed, and
# adding one would have normalised committing kubeconfigs.

# ── Untracked build artefacts and caches ────────────────────────────────────
# Retained only for the `scan-secrets-worktree` target, which scans the working tree
# rather than `git archive HEAD`. The committed-tree gate does not need these, because
# git archive emits tracked files only. Together they account for roughly 900 of the
# ~994 findings a naive full-tree scan returns, which is why an unscoped scan reads as
# catastrophic and a scoped one reads as clean.
^\.afm-image/
^ci-reports-2/
^ci-reports-2\.prev/
^\.cache/
^\.tmp/
^node_modules/
/node_modules/
__pycache__/
^\.git/
^\.venv/
/dist/
